.TH GG 1 2026-11-20
.SH NAME
gg \- a priority ledger and a budget clock for coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gg
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.PP
.B gg
.RB [ help | \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gg
keeps a ranked ledger of the big pieces of work a coding agent has been given.
Each item has an id, a title, a reason (what the user gains),
a time budget, and a status:
.BR queued ,
.BR active ,
.B parked
or
.BR done .
One item is active at a time.
Time spent on the active item is measured by
.B gg
outside the model.
.PP
The agent maintains the ledger itself through Claude Code hooks.
The user reads the ranking in the status line and corrects it with one sentence.
.PP
Each git repository has its own ledger.
Items that are not done are called open.
Rank is the position among open items, starting at 1.
.PP
Durations are written as 2h, 90m or 1h30m.
Any number followed by
.B h
or
.B m
counts, and the parts add up.
.PP
With no arguments,
.B gg
prints its help text.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "gg add " id " title " "\-\-why" " text " "\-\-budget" " dur"
Add an item at the bottom of the ranking with status queued.
The id, the title,
.B \-\-why
and
.B \-\-budget
are all required.
.TP
.BI "gg rank " "id id ..."
Move the listed items to the top of the ranking, in the order given.
The remaining items keep their relative order below them.
An unknown id is an error.
.TP
.BI "gg start " id
Set the item active and start its clock.
It fails if another item is already active.
.TP
.BI "gg park " "id note"
Stop the clock and set the item to parked.
The time spent so far is kept, and the note is stored as a hand-over.
Starting the item again resumes from the time already spent.
.TP
.BI "gg done " id
Close the item.
It no longer appears in the ranking.
If the item was active, its clock stops.
.TP
.BI "gg budget " "id dur"
Set the item's budget.
.TP
.B gg status
Print what the agent sees: a header with the time,
one entry per open item in rank order,
a warning when an unstarted queued item outranks the active one,
or the next item by rank when nothing is active,
and the rules.
An active item shows time spent against budget, and
.B OVER BUDGET
with the overrun when the budget is exceeded.
Prints nothing when there are no open items.
.TP
.RB "gg line [" dir "] [" \-\-session " " id ]
Print the status line row.
With
.I dir
it reads the ledger of the repository containing that directory
instead of the current one.
With
.B \-\-session
it uses the ledger remembered for that session when
.I dir
has none.
See
.BR "STATUS LINE" .
.TP
.B gg log
Print the history, one line per event: time, event name, item id and detail.
Events are add, rank, start, park, done and budget.
.TP
.B gg hook
Claude Code hook.
Reads the event JSON on stdin.
See
.BR HOOKS .
.TP
.B gg help
Print the help text.
.TP
.B gg man
Print this manual page as roff on stdout.
.SH HOOKS
.B gg hook
reads a JSON object on stdin and uses the fields
.IR hook_event_name ,
.I cwd
and
.IR stop_hook_active .
The ledger is the one for the repository containing
.IR cwd .
.TP
.B SessionStart
Prints the instructions that tell the agent how to keep the ledger.
If the repository has open items, it then prints the status.
.TP
.B UserPromptSubmit
Prints the status when there are open items.
Prints nothing when there is no ledger or no open item.
.TP
.B Stop
If an active item is over budget,
prints a JSON object on stdout that blocks the agent from ending its turn:
.RS
.PP
.nf
{"decision":"block","reason":"#<id> <title> is over budget: ..."}
.fi
.PP
The reason tells the agent to commit work in progress, run
.B gg park
on the item, and start the top-ranked queued item.
It also says to run
.B gg budget
instead if the user explicitly extended the budget.
.PP
When
.I stop_hook_active
is true, the hook prints nothing and the agent may stop.
It also prints nothing when there is no ledger or no item is over budget.
.RE
.SH SESSIONS
A session remembers the last ledger it saw,
so the status line and hooks keep working
when the session's directory leaves the repository.
A directory with its own ledger takes over.
.SH STATUS LINE
.B gg line
prints one row with the open items in rank order, separated by
.RB "\(dq\ \[u00B7]\ \(dq" .
.PP
Each entry starts with the rank number, then
.BI # id
and the title cut at 20 characters.
.IP \(bu 2
Queued items are plain:
.BR "2 #deps Bump dependencies" .
.IP \(bu 2
The active item is bold, with
.B \[u25B6]
after the rank number, followed by time spent and budget:
.BR "2\[u25B6] #deps Bump dependencies 40m/2h" .
.IP \(bu 2
An active item over budget is bold red and ends with
.BR OVER .
.IP \(bu 2
Parked items are dimmed and end with
.BR (parked) .
.PP
The output is empty when there are no open items.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GG_HOME
Directory that holds the ledgers.
Defaults to
.IR ~/.greater\-good .
.TP
.B GG_NOW
A fixed current time in the form
.BR 2006\-01\-02T15:04:05 ,
in local time.
Tests use it to control the clock.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.greater\-good/<repo path with / replaced by \->.json
The ledger of one git repository, as JSON.
Git worktrees share the ledger of their main repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B gg
exits 0 on success and 1 on error, with a message on stderr.
.B gg hook
always exits 0 and expresses a block as JSON on stdout.
.SH EXAMPLES
A short session:
.PP
.nf
.RS
gg add checkout "Fix checkout crash" \-\-why "users cannot pay" \-\-budget 4h
gg add deps "Bump dependencies" \-\-why "tidier lockfile" \-\-budget 1h
gg rank checkout deps
gg start checkout
gg park checkout "payment form fixed, tests missing"
gg start deps
gg done deps
.RE
.fi
.PP
Hooks in
.IR ~/.claude/settings.json ,
using the full path from
.BR "which gg" :
.PP
.nf
.RS
{
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart":     [{ "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/path/to/gg hook" }] }],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [{ "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/path/to/gg hook" }] }],
    "Stop":             [{ "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "/path/to/gg hook" }] }]
  }
}
.RE
.fi
.PP
Status line, where
.B $dir
is the session's working directory and
.B $session_id
is the
.I session_id
field of the status line input:
.PP
.nf
.RS
line=$(gg line "$dir" \-\-session "$session_id") && [ \-n "$line" ] && printf '%s\en' "$line"
.RE
.fi
